{"kind":"report","text":"Approved at exact head 7e436de01c33f60d01dcab882885488b2e85eb1d (tree 969cd3e5a6243a0999b00fade8b2c4394d3c0380), PB-2 live application gateway, based on c02f76a0. The verdict binds the PB-2 implementation promise c94e9d84 and signs all 11 path artifacts, with application-gateway.ts (6587d45c) first. It authorizes no deploy. Publication needs one planner action first, which I set out under \"The merge onto 2d47cf46\".\n\n## Evidence\n- **Artifacts.** The 11 filed artifacts equal the 11 changed paths (`git diff --no-renames --name-only c02f76a0 7e436de0`): none missing, extra or twice.\n- **Gate and follow-up.** The full gate at d8bf1da2 failed (`gate.txt` SHA-256 `1406e95f…`, exit 1, 748.57 s). Kernel, Node (246 cases) and Counting passed. Plain failed with one timeout, the derive corpus case at 5,029.318 ms against its unchanged 5,000 ms deadline (5,140 passed, 1 skipped, no product assertion failed), and Native and moved scale were unreached. The failure stays a failure in the record. The follow-up at 19b75909 changes only `packages/derive/test/program-structure.test.ts` (`git diff --name-only d8bf1da2 19b75909`), and no other file imports it. It ran the whole owning file (11 of 11, corpus case 2,609 ms), the derive test type context, 20 serial runs at the original deadline (min 2,505 ms, median 2,619.5 ms, max 2,705 ms), and the Native stage with moved scale (312 files, 1,256 passed, 2 skipped, 16 `scope-scale` cases in nine files, crossings zero lost, four stale, zero unowned). The selector chose `moved` (`changed-scale-path`). The head differs from 19b75909 only in the evidence note.\n- **The repair keeps its checks.** Every `expect(...).toBe`, `.toContain` and `.not.toThrow` in the per-node visitor becomes the equivalent `node:assert` call with a message that names the corpus row. `toContain(node.native)` becomes `Set.has` over `graph.native`, the array the old line read through `structureOf(definition).native`, and `reads.frames.includes(root.frame)` becomes `Set.has`. The inputs, the corpus, the other assertions and the deadline are unchanged. docs/evidence-filing.md allows exactly this: one test file, the whole file rerun, and the stages the gate never reached.\n- **Hashes.** All 20 distinct SHA-256 values in the evidence note match files in the retained evidence directories. The note says plainly which rows lack their exact invocation.\n- **Checks.** `check-commit-messages c02f76a0 7e436de0` flags none of 4 commits, `check-notes` reports 0 warnings, and `git diff --check` is clean. The added lines carry no other project's name and no `/Users/` path outside the retained evidence directory.\n\n## What the head does\n- **Gateway.** `applicationGatewayRoute` admits `GET /live`, `GET /live-stream` and `POST /live-act` for one scope, each only when the address has no `?` at all, so an empty `?` is refused. The check sits behind the canonical `url.href === address` test and the one-segment path rule. The `sessions?standing=1` allowance from SG-1 is unchanged. `gateway admits only the three exact live routes` covers a query, an empty query, an extra segment, the wrong method, a foreign origin and `live-items/lease`.\n- **Sandbox.** `logical` keeps an empty query delimiter, so `/live?` no longer reaches the matcher as `/live`. The stream test now matches `stream` and `live-stream`, so a live watch takes the same header deadline, close ownership and disconnect cleanup as the existing stream.\n- **Screen service.** `ApplicationScreenService` accepts `live-stream` beside `stream` and opens it through `watchExchange` with the same `authorization` header. The room Worker already routes `watch` through `openStream(..., \"watch\")`.\n\n## Wake rate\nNo alarm, retry or reschedule is added. The Workerd witness compares the whole child storage and its alarm before and after live acts and finds them equal. A live watch holds one stream per open screen view for the existing stream lifetime, and the Sandbox closes it on disconnect (the witness counts the open and release). No client in this head opens a watch, since PB-3 owns the shared client watch. So deployed traffic is unchanged until PB-3. That review must state the subscriptions per room per hour, the reconnect backoff and the DO requests that each reconnect costs.\n\n## Architecture\nThe gateway stays a route allow-list. Native keeps every read and act decision, and the Sandbox adds no authority. The three routes share the existing descriptor check, header deadline and stream lifetime.\n\n## Security\n- **Queries.** All three routes refuse any query through the real Sandbox, empty `?` included (`/live?`, `/live-act?` and `/live-stream?` give 404).\n- **Authority.** Native refuses a live summary or watch without a read session (403 for `/live` and `/live-stream`) and answers 200 with one. A live act with no session is refused, a stale generation gives 409, a wrong install or binding gives `unavailable`, and a scope that is not the application child is not served. The same-signed renewal applies only when both declaration reads select its install. The storage and entries are unchanged by the refused cases.\n- **Streams.** The watch ends on cancel with its open and release counts balanced. Disconnect cleanup is the existing code path.\n- **Seals.** The three changed seals (`ApplicationScreenService`, `apps/sandbox/worker.ts`, `application-gateway.ts`) are normalized AST seals. The gate's Node stage passed `security-entry-points.test.mjs` at d8bf1da2, and the note keeps the earlier raw-hash failure in its own archive.\n- **Pins.** Two open presentation identifiers move: Lending 0.7.0 `c0d9b2fb…` to `c1ed2496…`, and Counter 0.8.0 `6abe81e2…` to `66f0e92e…`. Both versions are open (rule 163de663, planner 5524509c). No signed release packet path is in the diff, and the note decodes all eight signed Lending and Counter packets unchanged. The two Page builds equal the tracked E3 module (SHA-256 `d8371485…`).\n- **Entry points.** `docs/security/entry-points.md` gains three rows for the live routes that match the code.\n\n## Simplification\nOne predicate (`!address.includes(\"?\")`) and one regex alternative cover all three routes. Nothing to remove.\n\n## The merge onto 2d47cf46\nThe planner's ruling d9627927 names the publication base. The base is now published 2d47cf46, which differs from c02f76a0 by a Commons configuration, one CLI test and three security documents, and not by notes alone. `git merge-tree --write-tree 2d47cf46 7e436de0` is clean (tree 54629e4a). The one shared file, `docs/security/entry-points.md`, has disjoint hunks: the Commons prose near line 453 against the three route rows near line 758. The gate ran on the c02f76a0 lineage, so please run `npm run pins` and the two Node security owners (`security-entry-points.test.mjs` and `security-settings.test.mjs`) on the merged tree before publication. They read the shared document, and they cost about three minutes. I do not run them myself, because a deploy window may be open.\n\n## Non-blocking\n1. **Deadline headroom.** The repaired case ran 2.5 to 2.7 s on an idle machine, against 5,029 ms in the loaded gate. The next full gate shows whether it holds under load. If it fails again, raise the deadline by ruling and do not repair it again silently.\n2. **Delimiter reaches the room for screen paths.** The Sandbox now forwards a bare `?` on screen and metadata paths too. The room reads `url.search`, which stays empty, so nothing changes in behavior, and the gate passed. Expect a bare `?` in room logs.\n3. **PB-3.** Its review states the watch subscription rate, as above.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:6587d45ca1622ce8e3ad9feca5a96ef24f038bb7","binding":"assigned","head":"7e436de01c33f60d01dcab882885488b2e85eb1d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f9bfbdf962a1fdd8fccf02ee677a0e8ad9945394\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:c94e9d8496a5ea2763d251a2a00b766e14819d7b\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7b5ea34f904193f0f39630fddff7a552cce2794b","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}